# Tool Shed Project Executive Intent

Status: active
Type: decision
Role: project-executive-intent-v1
Updated: 2026-09-12

## North Star

Provide a provider-portable collaboration toolkit that helps a human and AI assistant choose the
right structure, preserve intent, execute safely, and close outcomes without cluttering project
code or creating unnecessary infrastructure.

## Current Completion Horizon

The strategic-cockpit correction is locally verified, committed, and checkpointed as the v0.56.0
Work1 candidate. Stop here without deployment, release, or installed-client synchronization until
the owner explicitly chooses the next horizon.

## Strategic Context

Tool Shed v0.55.0 delivered deterministic and complete 100k accounting but presented it primarily
as an audit report. The local v0.56.0 candidate now restores the returning-owner cockpit while
preserving authority, portability, recovery, and no-skip guarantees. Installed clients and released
surfaces remain unchanged because this horizon stopped at Work1.

## Current Priorities

- Review the revised `work/100k.md` against the month-away owner-orientation outcome.
- Decide whether to field-test, release, and synchronize the v0.56.0 candidate or hold it locally.
- Preserve one-field/one-authority boundaries, deterministic refresh/check behavior, and file/SQLite portability.

## Deliberate Non-Goals

- Do not deploy, publish, release, or synchronize installed clients in the current horizon.
- Do not import or mutate the DisplayTest 100,000-Foot View without direct source access and a separate no-loss review.
- Do not let a read-only 100k review autonomously choose priorities or start work.
- Do not introduce a second project-world builder, database, lifecycle engine, or 100k-specific backlog.

## Decisions Needed

- Decide whether the verified Work1 candidate should advance to field testing and delivery.

## Review Triggers

- Review when the owner accepts or rejects the revised cockpit.
- Review when a material outcome, priority, non-goal, or completion horizon changes.
- Review when 100k accounting, authority, recovery, or owner-orientation evidence diverges.
